---
title: Specimen Parts
sidebar:
  label: Specimen parts
  order: 6
---

Use `Specimen Parts` for voucher preparations, tissues, swabs, parasites, and
other physical parts derived from the specimen. Each specimen can have multiple
parts.

The parasite tab is available for mammals, birds, herpetofauna, and fishes. It
is not available for invertebrate catalogs. For a fish lot with recorded
individuals, parts and parasites can be linked to the individuals they came
from; see [Fishes](/en/usages/specimens/measurements/fishes/#parts-and-parasites).

Part fields include:

- `Tissue ID`: optional tissue identifier. NAHPU can repeat or generate the next
  configured tissue number.
- `Individuals`: shown only for a fish lot with recorded individuals. Links the
  part to one or more individuals in the lot.
- `QR/barcode ID`: optional unique ID for a tube, tag, or container. On mobile,
  NAHPU can scan a QR/barcode; it can also generate a UUID.
- `Preparation type`: user-defined specimen part type.
- `Counts`: number of parts or containers.
- `Treatment`: preservation treatment.
- `Additional treatment`: optional second treatment.
- `Storage type`: storage medium or method.
- `Storage location`: freezer, cabinet, shelf, or container location.
- `Time taken`: time the part was taken, recommended for fresh tissues.
- `Preparator`: part-level preparator when different from the voucher preparator.
- `Date taken`: date the part was taken.
- `PMI`: post-mortem interval, for example `1:30`.
- `Museum permanent`: museum that permanently holds the part.
- `Museum loan`: museum receiving the part on loan.
- `Remarks`: notes specific to the part.

The part list displays the part type, count, barcode ID, preparator, tissue ID,
treatment, date/time, PMI, and whether a remark exists.

Parasite curation records carry their own `Storage` and `Storage location`
fields so the preservation method and physical location can be recorded
separately.
